-- Guarded content corrections: preserve locally edited rows and historical quiz snapshots.
UPDATE question_bank SET explanation='True. Plane angle (radian) and solid angle (steradian) are dimensionless derived SI units. The separate supplementary-unit category was abolished in 1995.' WHERE id='1f816852-190e-4a92-b1d6-d84aa63ddf5e' AND explanation='True. Plane angle (radian) and solid angle (steradian) are dimensionless quantities in terms of mass, length, and time ([M⁰ L⁰ T⁰]) but carry supplementary SI units.';
UPDATE question_bank SET question_text='A rocket starts from rest with initial mass M and ejects fuel at constant exhaust speed v_rel relative to the rocket. With no external forces, what is its speed after its mass decreases to M/2?' WHERE id='38f8d2b7-1fac-4e50-a033-32a8e1f064b9' AND question_text='A rocket of initial mass M ejects fuel gases at a constant relative exhaust velocity v_rel at rate dm/dt = α. In the absence of gravity, what is the rocket speed after its mass decreases to M/2?';
UPDATE question_bank SET explanation='The impulse-momentum theorem gives the magnitude of average stopping force as |Δp| / Δt. For the same momentum change, increasing stopping time reduces the average force; peak force also depends on the force-time profile.' WHERE id='fafb3a9b-997c-4bbe-9aea-bedc9184e0e1' AND explanation='From the impulse-momentum theorem: F = Δp / Δt. Increasing the contact time diminishes the peak stopping force exerted on the player’s palms.';
